@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "frontend"

Feature: Frontend Requests, Request Forms, and Request Comments
	Frontend testing for creating and viewing requests as well as request comments

Setup:
	* I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | Regular                    |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    | 
	| External ID      | Organization1              |
	* I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 2        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | Regular                    |
	| Support Region   | Japan                      |
	| Support Language | Japanese                   | 
	| External ID      | Organization2              |
	* I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 3        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | Regular                    |
	| Support Region   | Spain                      |
	| Support Language | Spanish                    | 
	| External ID      | Organization3              | 

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1  |
	| User2  |
	| Agent1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |
	| Organization2 |
	| Organization3 |

Scenario: Request Creation
	End users should be able to create and view a request using the Zendesk frontend.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            | 
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay DXP                             | 7.1                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Description" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1       |
	| Comment     | Request Description |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt      |

Scenario: Request Creation as User with Multiple Roles in Multiple Organizations
	End users should be able to create and view a request using the Zendesk frontend on only the organizations they are not a watcher of.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization2"
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization3"
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" as a watcher on an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1"
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" as a watcher on an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization2"	
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the Submit a ticket form
	And I click on the "Organization" dropdown
	Then I should see the following options
	| Organization Name 3 |
	And the following options should not be present
	| Organization Name 1 |
	| Organization Name 2 |
	When I go to the zendesk homepage
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay DXP                             | 7.1                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Organization  | Organization Name 3                                |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Description" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1       |
	| Comment     | Request Description |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt      |

Scenario: Request Comment
	End users should be able to create and view a comment on a request using the Zendesk frontend.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |  
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject |
	| Status        | OPEN            |
	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I submit a comment containing the following details
	| Comment     | Request Comment |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt  |
	Then I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Comment" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1   |
	| Comment     | Request Comment |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt  |
	And I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |

Scenario: Request Comment Positioning
	Request comments should be ordered from most recent to least.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |  
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	Then I should see a request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject |
	| Status        | OPEN            |
	When I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I submit a comment containing the following details
	| Comment     | Request Comment 1 |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt    |
	And I submit a comment containing the following details
	| Comment     | Request Comment 2 |
	| Attachments | Document_2.txt    |
	And I submit a comment containing the following details
	| Comment     | Request Comment 3 |
	| Attachments | Document_3.txt    |
	Then I should be able to view a request comment in position number "1" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1     |
	| Comment     | Request Comment 3 |
	| Attachments | Document_3.txt    |
	And I should be able to view a request comment in position number "2" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1     |
	| Comment     | Request Comment 2 |
	| Attachments | Document_2.txt    |
	And I should be able to view a request comment in position number "3" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1     |
	| Comment     | Request Comment 1 |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt    |
	And I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |

Scenario: Request Assignee
	End users should be able to view a ticket's assignee on a request using the Zendesk frontend.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                      |
	| Language         | English                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CAS - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" 
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Assigned to   | Zendesk Agent1                                     |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: Mark Request as Solved
	Requesters should be able to mark a request as solved.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                      |
	| Language         | English                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CAS - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" 
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I mark the request as solved
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | SOLVED                                             |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Assigned to   | Zendesk Agent1                                     |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |

Scenario: Mark Request as Solved with Comment
	Requesters should be able to mark a request as solved with a comment.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                      |
	| Language         | English                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CAS - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" 
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I mark the request as solved with a comment containing the following details
	| Comment     | Request Comment |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt  |	
