	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Comment" with the following details
	| Author      | Zendesk User1   |
	| Comment     | Request Comment |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt  |

Scenario: View Closed Request
	Closed requests should only contain certain options.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                      |
	| Language         | English                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CAS - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I change the status and sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solved" and "completed" respectively
	And I assign a ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" with the following tags
	| auto_closed |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | SOLVED                                             |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Assigned to   | Zendesk Agent1                                     |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | Completed                                          |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	And I should not see the request comment field
	And I should see the closed comment message
	And I should not see the large attachment link

Scenario: Create Follow Up
	End users should be able to create a follow up on a closed ticket.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk Agent1                    |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                     |
	| Role             | Agent                             |
	| Email            | zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                      |
	| Language         | English                           |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)        |
	| External ID      | Agent1                            |
	And I assign the user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken" to the group "CAS - US"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "zendesk.agent1@liferay.com.broken"
	And I change the status and sub-status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "solved" and "completed" respectively
	And I assign a ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" with the following tags
	| auto_closed |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to My activities
	And I click on the request with the subject "Request Subject" in the index
	And I create a follow-up request
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Re: Request Subject                                |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | Zendesk User1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay DXP > 7.1                                  |
	| Sub-Status    | Completed                                          |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	And I should see the request comment field
	And I should not see the closed comment message
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "This is a follow-up to your previous request" with the following details
	| Author          | Zendesk User1                                |
	| Partial Comment | This is a follow-up to your previous request |
	| Partial Comment | "Request Subject"                            |

Scenario: Watcher Permissions
	End users who are watchers in an organization should not be able to create a request for their organization or add comments on any request for their organization.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User2                    |
	| Tags             | osb_kb                           |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user2@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User2                            |
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product                  | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
	| Component                | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status            | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject                  | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description              | Request Description                              |
	| Organization External ID | Organization1                                    |
