Scenario: Ticket Form Validation for Multiple Organizations
	End users should be able to see all available products in the Product dropdown field for a given organization when submitting a request.

	Given I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	And I assign a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" to an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization2"
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| liferay_dxp_cloud       |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization2" with the following tags
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| liferay_analytics_cloud |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I go to the Submit a ticket form
	And I click on the "Organization" dropdown
	And I click the option "Organization Name 1"
	And I click on the "Product" dropdown
	Then I should see the following options
	| Developer Tools           |
	| Liferay DXP               |
	| Liferay DXP Cloud         |
	| Liferay Portal            |
	| Mobile Experience         |
	| Productivity Tools (Sync) |
	And the following options should not be visible
	| Liferay Analytics Cloud   |
	| Liferay Commerce          |
	| Management Tools (LCS)    |
	When I click the option "-"
	And I click on the "Organization" dropdown
	And I click the option "Organization Name 2"
	And I click on the "Product" dropdown
	Then I should see the following options
	| Liferay Analytics Cloud   |
	| Liferay Commerce          |
	| Liferay DXP               |
	| Liferay Portal            |
	| Management Tools (LCS)    |
	And the following options should not be visible
	| Developer Tools           |
	| Liferay DXP Cloud         |
	| Mobile Experience         |
	| Productivity Tools (Sync) |

